UnicodeMathML: a decimal comma only on request (options.decimalComma)

UnicodeMath reads both "." and "," as a decimal separator, so `{1,2,3}`
became the numbers 1,2 and ,3 rather than a set of three. Mathessible lets the
user choose (setting `decimal_separator`): with `decimalComma: false` in
the converter options, "," is never part of a number and `{1,2,3}` is a
list; with it true (the default, as upstream), `1,5` is a number and a
list needs a space, `{1, 2, 3}`. The parser rule `opDecimal` checks the
option (the generated dist parser by hand, the .pegjs to match), and
`parse` passes the converter's option on to the parser.

Applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh on top of the UnicodeMathML submodule.

